---
import LegalPageLayout from '../components/LegalPageLayout.astro';
import { legalPageLastUpdated, privacyServices } from '../data/legal';
import { getPageMetadata } from '../data/metadata';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const metadata = getPageMetadata({
  title: 'Privacy | Gizlet',
  description: 'How Gizlet handles local tool processing, analytics, and advertising.',
  pathname: '/privacy/',
});
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <LegalPageLayout
    eyebrow="Gizlet policy"
    title="Privacy"
    introduction="A clear account of what Gizlet processes in your browser and what separately configured services may receive."
  >
    <h2>Local Gizlets</h2>
    <p>
      When a Gizlet is marked <strong>Local</strong> on its tool page, the file or text you provide to that
      Gizlet is processed in your browser on this device. Gizlet does not upload that marked tool input to a
      Gizlet server for the tool to do its job.
    </p>
    <p>
      This promise is specific to Gizlets marked Local. It is not a blanket claim about every current or future
      Gizlet, and it does not prevent separate analytics or advertising requests described below.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics and advertising are separate from Gizlet processing. They are disabled during development and
      only added to a production build when their public configuration is enabled. The current provider details
      are listed below so they can stay in step with the services Gizlet uses.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        privacyServices.map((service) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{service.category}: </strong>
            <a href={service.url}>{service.name}</a>: {service.description}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      Plausible may receive page URL, referrer, browser, operating system, device type, and country for
      aggregate reporting. Google and its advertising partners may process a page request and information needed
      to serve and measure ads. Where required, Gizlet will provide the relevant consent choices before serving
      advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>What Gizlet does not send as analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Gizlet does not send file contents, filenames, file sizes, dimensions, formats, JSON contents, generated
      passwords, tool results, error messages, or other entered or generated tool payloads in its analytics
      events. Gizlet’s defined tool events contain only a static tool slug.
    </p>

    <h2>Gizlet requests</h2>
    <p>
      The request-a-Gizlet form does not send its idea, use case, or optional contact field to Gizlet. It prepares
      a new issue on GitHub for you to review and submit yourself. If you continue and submit that issue, GitHub
      handles the information under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this page when Gizlet’s tools or configured providers change. The current provider list and
      descriptions above will be updated with the service change.
    </p>
    <p class="metadata">Last updated {legalPageLastUpdated}</p>
  </LegalPageLayout>
</BaseLayout>
